      "role": "user",
      "content": "The lab results are pretty specific though. It's not just a tiny trace—the readings show a synthetic polymer that wasn't even invented until the mid-19th century. If that binder is widespread, it's not just a \"restoration\" issue, it's a whole different era. Given how much is riding on this piece for the Q4 auction, I need your honest take: are we looking at a genuine masterpiece with some heavy-handed repairs, or is this a total forgery that's going to blow up in our faces if we put it in the catalog?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
