      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A widespread presence of a mid-19th-century synthetic polymer signals a significant issue beyond routine restoration; it raises serious questions about the object's integrity. At this point, you must proceed with extreme caution, as replicating such widespread an altering material strongly suggests the piece is not original to the Dutch Golden Age. I recommend halting further public cataloging until a senior conservation expert can undertake a high-level assessment to definitively classify the object's origin.",
